# Hostile audit — Target C exact four-host Type-II capacity dichotomy

**Date:** 2026-09-13  
**Artifact:** `target_c_four_host_typeii_capacity_dichotomy_2026-09-12.md`  
**State lock:** `2026-09-12.audit.46`  
**Verdict:** PASS at the stated proof-only scope; no C-II closure.

## 1. Host-width equality

For a host `q` in the closed unit disk, `q·u=1` forces `q=u`, and `q·u=-1`
forces `q=-u`. Therefore width two in each of two nonparallel train directions
does require the four hosts `+u,-u,+v,-v`. The zero host contributed by a closed
exceptional-face route does not affect this equality.

The report's geometric hypothesis is stronger than merely saying that four hosts
are available: after removing repeated collinear attachment vertices, the only
nonzero consecutive-attachment directions are those four directions. This distinction
is necessary because additional hosts can leave both widths equal to two.

**Verdict:** pass.

## 2. Four directions imply a parallelogram

A nondegenerate convex polygon whose edge directions lie in
`{+u,-u,+v,-v}` has, after suppressing collinear intermediate vertices, one edge in
each direction. Closure forces opposite side vectors to cancel, so the polygon is a
parallelogram. Repeated attachment vertices on one side do not change the convex
polygon and are harmless for the area argument.

**Verdict:** pass; no unsupported simplicity assumption is needed.

## 3. Near-disk parallelogram calculation

The Type-II near-disk input supplies, after translating the force-hull center to the
origin, a common radius `R_D=D/2` and `epsilon_D->0` with all attachment vertices in
the annulus `R_D+/-epsilon_D D`. Writing the four corners as
`c_D +/- r_D +/- s_D`, differences of squared norms give

`c_D·r_D=o(D^2)`, `c_D·s_D=o(D^2)`, and `r_D·s_D=o(D^2)`.

For a macroscopic area lower bound, `|r_D x s_D|=Omega(D^2)`, while `|r_D|,|s_D|=O(D)`.
The first two scalar estimates then imply `|c_D|=o(D)` by inverting the two-dimensional
Gram system; the determinant is bounded below by the cross product. Averaging the four
corner squared norms gives

`|r_D|^2+|s_D|^2=R_D^2+o(D^2)`.

Finally `4|r_D x s_D| <= 2(|r_D|^2+|s_D|^2)` gives
`area(P_D)<=D^2/2+o(D^2)`. The same macroscopic lower bound and `|r_D|,|s_D|=O(D)`
give a linear inradius, so the `o(D)` center displacement places the hull origin in
the polygon interior for all sufficiently large `D`.

**Verdict:** pass. The area estimate is asymptotic and is not claimed for small cells.

## 4. At most one macroscopic exact four-host cell

Canonical attachment-cell disjointness gives disjoint interiors. Every exact four-host
cell with area at least `eta D^2` contains the common force-hull center in its interior.
Two such cells therefore contradict disjoint interiors. The argument does not require
their boundaries to be disjoint.

**Verdict:** pass.

## 5. Small-cell tail and positive-area alternative

The canonical cell budget

`sum_r sqrt(area(P_r))=O(D)`

is the relevant Section-83 consequence. For cells with area below `eta D^2`,

`area(P_r) <= sqrt(eta) D sqrt(area(P_r))`,

so their total area is `O(sqrt(eta)D^2)`. Since the Type-II cell areas sum to
`(pi/4-o(1))D^2`, choose fixed `eta>0` small enough that this tail cannot fill the
gap between `1/2` and `pi/4`. If every remaining macroscopic cell were exact four-host,
there would be at most one of them and its area would be at most `D^2/2+o(D^2)`.
Thus a cell of area at least `eta D^2` outside the exact four-host class exists.

The coefficient hidden in the `O(sqrt(eta))` budget is finite and depends only on the
canonical Section-83 bound, so an explicit numerical `eta` is unnecessary for this
compactness statement.

**Verdict:** pass.

## 6. Scope and remaining gate

This is a capacity restriction on the exact four-host regression only. It does not
prove that the non-four-host cell has positive width defect: an additional host can
contain the same four antipodal directions. It also does not identify the remaining
cell with a global minimizer competitor or create a unit equilateral triangle.
Contact-isolated source points are not deleted and no full-source affine-kernel claim
is used.

**Final classification:** audited-working proof-only bridge. The theorem state remains
unchanged and C-II remains open.
